                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "393ae424-b718-3190-8f11-d7bf8dd803f5",
                        "entry_id": "861529e7-e3c4-3950-a77d-95eed6309fe6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Découpé, entamé comme si on en avait emporté une pièce avec des ciseaux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2c40ded-541f-4538-9202-4f5acebcaccd",
                                "sense_id": "393ae424-b718-3190-8f11-d7bf8dd803f5",
                                "text": "Des feuilles échancrées en forme de croissant, en cœur, en pointe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b5ecac1-0396-415c-93f9-6c8a8d108bef",
                                "sense_id": "393ae424-b718-3190-8f11-d7bf8dd803f5",
                                "text": "Pétales échancrés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a03f040d-9828-4d13-8255-ea5a959e0def",
                                "sense_id": "393ae424-b718-3190-8f11-d7bf8dd803f5",
                                "text": "Les côtes de la Bretagne sont très profondément échancrées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad2f040a-739b-4250-97e4-31f976758837",
                                "sense_id": "393ae424-b718-3190-8f11-d7bf8dd803f5",
                                "text": "Les Indiens coupent dans les bois des bambous qu'ils réunissent avec des lianes ou des herbes suffisamment résistantes, et au moyen de ces échelles improvisées, on parvient à escalader les obstacles. … D'autres se composent simplement d’un arbre posé verticalement, et échancré de distance en distance de façon à permettre d'y appuyer le bout des pieds."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4df4057-ac2e-38d2-9b5e-b3a25c878281",
                        "entry_id": "861529e7-e3c4-3950-a77d-95eed6309fe6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractérise des lames de champignons formant une échancrure autour du pied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1af23f93-432b-490c-9bb3-488434b747e0",
                                "sense_id": "e4df4057-ac2e-38d2-9b5e-b3a25c878281",
                                "text": "Les tricholomes ont des lames échancrées."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9331d6d-d504-3a79-82b3-dea7bd252481",
                        "entry_id": "861529e7-e3c4-3950-a77d-95eed6309fe6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est très découpé, qui laisse voir de la peau, voire qui est suggestif (en parlant d'un vêtement et particulièrement des sous-vêtements ou tenues de bain)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "737557df-994b-4ae6-9872-20f8354cecd8",
                                "sense_id": "e9331d6d-d504-3a79-82b3-dea7bd252481",
                                "text": "Il porte la redingote, la cravate blanche, un faux col largement échancré."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c44e0950-00f9-401a-b9a2-ccef7295ac99",
                                "sense_id": "e9331d6d-d504-3a79-82b3-dea7bd252481",
                                "text": "Au milieu des bibelots alignés sur la commode de bois ciré trône la photographie de Doris prise en maillot de bain échancré, à l’arrière d'un yacht."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c13349e-91f0-415d-9ab0-3552293b2134",
                        "source_entry_id": "861529e7-e3c4-3950-a77d-95eed6309fe6",
                        "source_sense_description": "mycologie",
                        "target_lang_word": "emarginate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "emarginate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e7cfde3-5da5-32f4-8107-9dc8208ce62e",
                                        "entry_id": "91d4e6e1-e592-30c9-9d44-c295bb685ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With the outline of the margin more or less concave in places, usually at the apex."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of leaves"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1720cea-70f6-3c34-a89c-416aafcdb40b",
                                        "entry_id": "91d4e6e1-e592-30c9-9d44-c295bb685ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having roughly the same height or width for most of its length, becoming much shallower or narrower before reaching the attachment point."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78de156e-738d-47b6-a0db-1f02ee71fbe1",
                                                "sense_id": "b1720cea-70f6-3c34-a89c-416aafcdb40b",
                                                "text": "In this group of mushrooms, the attachment of the gills to the stipe is emarginate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8961537d-3104-3dee-b96a-8839b08db720",
                                        "entry_id": "91d4e6e1-e592-30c9-9d44-c295bb685ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a margin that has concave edges as though with parts removed or notched."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a2926f6-9e24-4dac-b790-72597b5f5f0c",
                                                "sense_id": "8961537d-3104-3dee-b96a-8839b08db720",
                                                "text": "1840 Georges Cuvier Cuvier's Animal kingdom (intranslation).\nIn the Haliotus, Lam, the shell is perforated along the side of the columella with a series of holes; and when the last hole remains incomplete, the shell has the appearance of beiing emarginate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3b7f1a7-9938-3bc6-9284-c287c1aa0b05",
                                        "entry_id": "91d4e6e1-e592-30c9-9d44-c295bb685ebc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a crystal: having edges or corners of the primitive form beveled, crossed by a face."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "emarginate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbe73261-3421-3725-a875-797adea5de9a",
                                        "entry_id": "93929cb4-dba2-328b-b876-a8cb35601105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take away the margin of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e51da022-b414-4e2b-abbf-aa1253c25b49",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe73261-3421-3725-a875-797adea5de9a",
                                                "text": "The radius resembles that of Nesodon in form, but is proportionately shorter and stouter; the distal end is especially massive and the scaphoid facet emarginates the dorsal border more deeply and in a more conspicuous way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44fbf279-a1d7-45fc-92be-a4d351dfa257",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe73261-3421-3725-a875-797adea5de9a",
                                                "text": "a radial depression extends from the beak to the anterior ventral margin, which it slightly emarginates;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a88b3671-8e03-48e8-95a1-68e76b377999",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe73261-3421-3725-a875-797adea5de9a",
                                                "text": "At most, the groove emarginates only one-third the distal surface of the femur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f01672b-af6f-3239-b141-8769714c5204",
                                        "entry_id": "93929cb4-dba2-328b-b876-a8cb35601105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lose the margin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "503439e6-7a0e-4e48-9772-fb560e5c833e",
                                                "sense_id": "0f01672b-af6f-3239-b141-8769714c5204",
                                                "text": "The palate in Leptictis emarginates between M's."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74076092-8732-4d9e-953e-7c5fecf067c1",
                                                "sense_id": "0f01672b-af6f-3239-b141-8769714c5204",
                                                "text": "This membrane emarginates at intervals, forming pits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2e50899-d149-41d2-aeec-050b5681fde5",
                                                "sense_id": "0f01672b-af6f-3239-b141-8769714c5204",
                                                "text": "The body shape is mostly circular in stage 1, then becomes elongated, and the hindbody emarginates at later stages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ad43482-4aa6-3659-8b43-c67266824d9a",
                                        "entry_id": "93929cb4-dba2-328b-b876-a8cb35601105",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To marginalize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e530cec6-0305-48e2-9137-79657432318d",
                                                "sense_id": "4ad43482-4aa6-3659-8b43-c67266824d9a",
                                                "text": "Hegel ignores, represses, and emarginates these factors in order to found his logic on a dialectic conceived as the appropriation of the other, rather than a becoming other (Anderswerden)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b35c626-e29c-4a76-aa65-e91a18194e90",
                                                "sense_id": "4ad43482-4aa6-3659-8b43-c67266824d9a",
                                                "text": "Indeed, it has been argued that the theory of Anglo conformity is inherently discriminatory: it requires assimilation into a majoritarian culture and inferentially emarginates other legitimate forms of cultural expression ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88d1383e-bff5-491d-b0be-6b0e97be7399",
                                                "sense_id": "4ad43482-4aa6-3659-8b43-c67266824d9a",
                                                "text": "The economic process, then, converges in that space and emarginates whole categories of residents from zones rendered inaccessible to them because they are beyond their financial means."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bf4cd54-ca84-4811-bd17-19ee46ba65c0",
                                                "sense_id": "4ad43482-4aa6-3659-8b43-c67266824d9a",
                                                "text": "Their antisocial behavior may be a conscious or subconscious act against a system that they feel to be uncaring and oppressive, and that, in their opinion, emarginates them from the mainstream of society."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c91de030-5712-425f-b7fd-09a4d0f486e5",
                        "source_entry_id": "861529e7-e3c4-3950-a77d-95eed6309fe6",
